DESCRIPTION >
    Daily BYOP app usage split by whether the spending user is the app owner.
    byop_app_daily cannot answer this: it aggregates spenders into a uniq state,
    so owner self-spend is indistinguishable from a real user paying in the app.
    Quests that must not be self-awardable read this instead.

    owner_user_id leads the sorting key because every read is a single-owner
    lookup; generation_event_v2 sorts by start_time, which makes the equivalent
    raw-table scan read the whole history per request.

TOKEN "tinybird_read" READ

SCHEMA >
    `day` Date,
    `environment` LowCardinality(String),
    `owner_user_id` String,
    `is_external` Bool,
    `billed_paid_calls` AggregateFunction(sum, UInt64),
    `gross_consumption` AggregateFunction(sum, Float64)

ENGINE AggregatingMergeTree
ENGINE_PARTITION_KEY toYYYYMM(day)
ENGINE_SORTING_KEY owner_user_id, day, environment, is_external
